<header><p class="st-kicker">tribal confederation · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Pogesanians</h1><p class="st-meta">800 CE – 1274 CE (approx.)</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Prussian people between the Elbląg and Pasłęk rivers, whose land saw the founding of Elbing and fierce fighting in the Great Prussian Uprising.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>Pogesania lay along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula-lagoon">Vistula Lagoon</a> east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elblag">Elbląg</a> river, in modern northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>. Its Prussian inhabitants lived near the old trading centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/truso">Truso</a>, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a> emporium described by the traveller Wulfstan around 890, and they are known from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-of-dusburg">Peter of Dusburg's</a> chronicle.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Pogesanian society was led by nobles holding hillforts, with farming, fishing and the amber trade as mainstays. They kept the Prussian gods and customs, including cremation of the dead, which Wulfstan described in detail.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> and the Hanseatic settlers of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-and-hanseatic-city-of-lubeck">Lübeck</a> founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elblag">Elbing</a> on their land in 1237. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-prussian-uprising">Great Prussian Uprising</a> from 1260 the Pogesanians, led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/auktume">Auktume</a>, attacked Elbing and other castles, but they were subdued by 1274. Their territory became part of the Order's state.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/pogesanians.jpg" alt="Pogesanians" width="320" height="306"><figcaption>Image: JakaśKreatywnaNazwa123 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pogezania_na_mapie_adm._Polski.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>800 CE – 1274 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>tribal confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Auktume</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Baltic paganism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Old Prussian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/poland">Poland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Pogesania, Pagude</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1037&amp;focus=pogesanians" aria-label="Pogesanians on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5108 379 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Pogesanians lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5451 561h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5428 635h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5428 635h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Poland. <a href="/atlas?year=1037&amp;focus=pogesanians">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

